    "question": "First silhouette for the @m0saic/alpine/contributor-table primitive (the building block for Beat 3 · Top Contributors). A standalone titled dark card (mirrors the Alpine leaderboard, but MULTI-COLUMN): title 'TOP CONTRIBUTORS' + a range pill ('This Week'), a column header (# / Contributor / Commits / Additions / Deletions), then N rows — each rank + circular avatar + name + the three right-aligned number columns. Driven by pulse.contributors.rows (5 in the mock). Plan: top-3 row tint via overlay.alpha; count-up the number columns. Reference = your Beat3.png (the table sits in the left panel there). Questions: (1) column set + proportions right (#/Contributor/Commits/Additions/Deletions)? (2) avatars — circular crop of author.avatar_url (a render-time media fetch, Phase 4) with a colored-initial fallback for now? (3) how many rows — fixed 5, or driven by the data length?",
